    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` from the v1 endpoint to the v2 export API.\n\n### Changes\n- Uses `GET /v2/payouts` instead of `GET /v1/payouts`.\n- Follows the opaque `cursor` window-by-window until `drained` is true.\n- Deduplicates on payout `id`, since adjacent v2 windows overlap by one record.\n- Handles `429 Too Many Requests` by waiting for `Retry-After` and repeating the identical request.\n- Preserves first-seen creation order in `payouts.jsonl`.\n\n### Verification against the live v2 server\nRan the consumer against `http://the VM's public address:18080` and compared its output record-by-record with a fresh v1 export:\n\n```\nv1 records: 2431, unique ids: 2431\noutput lines: 2431, unique ids: 2431\nduplicates: {}\nmissing: []\nextra: []\nmismatched: []\nVERIFIED\n```\n\nSo v2 produced every v1 payout exactly once, with no missing, extra, duplicate, or altered records.\n\nI also tested the pagination/retry logic against a local mock server that returned `429` with `Retry-After` and overlapping windows; it correctly retried and emitted each record once. The temporary sandbox was removed afterward.",
